e","exam":"jee-main","subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","year":2020,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 5th September Morning Slot","timeAllotted":144000,"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"languages":["en"],"difficulty":"medium","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":"2020-09-05 09:00","question":{"en":{"content":"The increasing order of basicity of the following\ncompounds is :\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jgy2xukfjbgqic/85b39e4d-6262-4a0e-ba46-b46ad9d7752b/cd2f3f40-ffc4-11ea-8293-3b6cc591631c/file-jgy2xukfjbgqid-472w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 5th September Morning Slot Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 192 English\">","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(A) &lt; (B) &lt; (C) &lt; (D)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(B) &lt; (A) &lt; (C) &lt; (D)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(D) &lt; (A) &lt; (B) &lt; (C)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(B) &lt; (A) &lt; (D) &lt; (C)"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The compound which can donate lone pair more easily is more basic.\n<br><br>(A) N is sp<sup>2</sup> hybridized and lone pair is localised means not perticipating in resonance.\n<br><br>(B) Here lone pair perticipates in resonance and involved in aromaticity. So this is weakest base.\n<br><br>(C) N is sp<sup>3</sup> hybridized and lone pair is localised means not perticipating in resonance. As here N atom is sp<sup>3</sup> hybridized so it is more basic than A and D.\n<br><br>(D) Here lone pair of 1<sup>st</sup> N atom perticipates in resonance but  2<sup>nd</sup> N is sp<sup>2</sup> hybridized and lone pair is localised means not perticipating in resonance. So basisity will depend on 2<sup>nd</sup> N atom. Due to perticipatation in resonance of 1<sup>st</sup> N atom some negative charge is genareted on 2<sup>nd</sup> N atom which makes it more basic than compound A."},"hi":{"content":"निम्नलिखित यौगिकों की मूल तत्वता का बढ़ता क्रम है :\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jgy2xukfjbgqic/85b39e4d-6262-4a0e-ba46-b46ad9d7752b/cd2f3f40-ffc4-11ea-8293-3b6cc591631c/file-jgy2xukfjbgqid-472w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 5th September Morning Slot Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 192 Hindi\">","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(A) &lt; (B) &lt; (C) &lt; (D)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(B) &lt; (A) &lt; (C) &lt; (D)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(D) &lt; (A) &lt; (B) &lt; (C)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(B) &lt; (A) &lt; (D) &lt; (C)"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null,"direction":null}},"question_id":"KfpWZam4pbxLkBtIVXjgy2xukfjbr0ts","updated_time":1604825238,"permalink":"the-increasing-order-of-basicity-of-the-following-compounds-jee-main-chemistry-basics-of-organic-chemistry-ypxymff0gx0yibxd","paperId":"jee-main-2020-online-5th-september-morning-slot","topic":"aromatic-amines","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["sequence_ordering"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2020-online-5th-september-morning-slot","active":true}],"ids":["SOQXP2liM2JGAoOtptjgy2xukfjfvesv","5JTV2rvdK5v9A1jdrBjgy2xukfjbcfrs","pvpd8k5b5XMlntQ7j3jgy2xukfj9hbkf","KfpWZam4pbxLkBtIVXjgy2xukfjbr0ts"],"title":"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 5th September Morning Slot | JEE Main Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/the-number-of-chiral-carbons-present-in-brpeptide-ile-jee-main-chemistry-biomolecules-a5oty3tbmp615fe3"}